# Python that builds every .ankiaddon (read via setup-python's
# python-version-file by every workflow job that runs package.sh, and by
# package.sh itself, which refuses to build on any other version). It must
# match the Python Anki ships: 3.13 for Anki 25.07+.
#
# `pip download --python-version 313` only selects wheel tags. pip still
# evaluates environment markers such as anyio's
# `typing_extensions>=4.16.0; python_version < "3.15"` against THIS interpreter,
# so any other build Python vendors different versions -- 0.41.0 was built on
# 3.15 and shipped an anyio that cannot load inside Anki.
#
# Not named .python-version on purpose: pyenv/uv would pick that up locally.
# No inline comments: setup-python only skips lines that start with #.
3.13
